ic\">white</span> portland cement, <span class=\"italic\">any color</span> is available in stucco—from pure white, through pastel tints of cream and salmon and tan and pink, to rich warm yellows and browns and greens and other shades. <span class=\"bullet\">●</span> Durability, texture, color—these are selling points for stucco that help convince your prospects of a home's desirability—and that mean ready turnover and profit to you. Want the details? Write Universal Atlas Cement Co. (<span class=\"italic\">United States Steel Corporation Subsidiary</span>), 208 South LaSalle Street, Chicago.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"atlas-heading\">\n    <span class=\"small-num\">210</span>\n    <h2>STUCCO <span class=\"made-with\">made with</span> ATLAS WHITE</h2>\n    <div class=\"sub-line\">PORTLAND CEMENT</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"image-section\">\n    <div class=\"house-image\">\n      <div class=\"placeholder\">[Photograph: A trim stucco home with striped awnings, arched doorway, and steps]</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"image-caption\">\n      <span class=\"dot\">●</span>\n      This trim and tidy home has been modernized with an Atlas White portland cement stucco finish in a semi-rough texture.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
